EXT. COMMERCIAL WAREHOUSE - STORMY NIGHT

SUPER: "LAST QUARTER..."

A drone glides low over an expansive flat industrial roof.
Storm water pools in wide black sheets. A membrane seam has
split — a dark wound running six feet across the surface.

INT. WAREHOUSE - SAME NIGHT

SUPER: "$80,000 IN INVENTORY. ONE ROOF FAILURE."

FACILITIES MANAGER (50s, pressed shirt, name badge) stands
under a rack of industrial shelving. He looks up. Water drips
steadily into a yellow emergency bucket. His jaw tightens.

SUPER: "STORM SHIELD ROOFING — CALLED AT 6 AM."

EXT. COMMERCIAL WAREHOUSE - EARLY MORNING

A heavy-duty white fleet truck — "Storm Shield Roofing
Commercial Division" — pulls to the loading dock. A COMMERCIAL
CREW OF FOUR in safety vests deploys immediately: ladders,
TPO welding equipment, industrial sealant kits.

EXT. FLAT ROOF - CONTINUOUS

SUPER: "COMMERCIAL-GRADE. SAME-DAY."

The LEAD TECHNICIAN runs a thermal scan across the membrane.
Crew seals the breach with industrial TPO. Drains cleared.
Seams heat-welded. Roof restored to spec.

INT. WAREHOUSE - LATER THAT DAY

SUPER: "BACK IN OPERATION. ZERO INVENTORY LOST."

The FACILITIES MANAGER stands at his desk, reviewing the
inspection report on a tablet. He signs off — satisfied,
composed. His facility is secure.

SUPER: "STORM SHIELD ROOFING — COMMERCIAL DIVISION"
SUPER: "Licensed • Bonded • OSHA Compliant"
SUPER: "StormShieldRoofing.com/commercial | (800) 555-ROOF"

